---
description: One-pass execution budget for repository work
alwaysApply: true
---

# One pass

- Run one batched search, then read the relevant files in parallel.
- Do not reopen a file or a successful command, and do not summarize intermediate checks.
- Implement in one pass. Do not start a second exploration, review pass, or subagent.
- Run one relevant package test after implementation, then run `pnpm run verify` once as the final gate.
- On failure, fix the reported cause, rerun only the failed package, then run `pnpm run verify` once more.
- Ponytail and Caveman apply in full. This rule limits tool calls only.

## Command output

- Redirect complete test and verification output to a temporary log outside the repository.
- On success, read and report only the command and `PASS`. Do not inspect the log.
- On failure, report the command, exit code, failed package or check, and the smallest error block that identifies the cause.
- Do not load the full failure log. Expand the error context only when the first block is insufficient to diagnose the cause.
